    5 ## 2.1. CAN ID Structure (29-bit Extended)
    6 
    7 The 29-bit CAN ID is structured to convey priority, message type, source, and destination, enabling robust filtering and routing.
    8 
    9 | Bits       | Length | Field Name         | Description                                                 |
   10 |------------|--------|--------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
   11 | 28-26      | 3 bits | Priority           | Message priority (0 = highest, 7 = lowest).                 |
   12 | 25-24      | 2 bits | Message Type       | Defines the purpose of the frame (see table below).         |
   13 | 23-16      | 8 bits | Destination Address| Address of the recipient node.                              |
   14 | 15-8       | 8 bits | Source Address     | Address of the sender node.                                 |
   15 | 7-0        | 8 bits | Reserved           | Reserved for future use (must be 0).                        |
   16 
   17 ### Message Types
   18 
   19 | Value (binary) | Name    | Description                                       |
   20 |----------------|---------|---------------------------------------------------|
   21 | `00`           | `COMMAND` | A command from the host to a device.                |
   22 | `01`           | `ACK`     | Positive acknowledgment of a command.             |
   23 | `10`           | `NACK`    | Negative acknowledgment (error).                  |
   24 | `11`           | `DATA`    | Data packet from a device to the host.            |
   25 | `11`           | `DONE`    | Frame indicating the end of command execution. |
   26 | `11`           | `LOG`     | Asynchronous log message from a device.           |
   27 
   28 **Note**: `DATA`, `DONE`, and `LOG` share the same `Message Type` code. They will be differentiated by a sub-type field within the data payload (see section 2.2).
   29 
   30 ### Node Addresses
   31 
   32 A table of node addresses should be maintained here.
   33 
   34 | Address (hex) | Node Name                | Description                                |
   35 |---------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
   36 | `0x00`        | Broadcast                | All nodes.                                 |
   37 | `0x01`        | Host Controller (PC)     | The main controlling computer.             |
   38 | `0x10`        | Conductor (This Device)  | The STM32H723 main board.                  |
   39 | `0x20`        | Dispenser Node 1         | Example исполнитель on STM32F103.           |
   40 | ...           | ...                      | ...                                        |
