    2 ## 3.2. Sub-Payload Structures
    3 
    4 As defined in `2_Frame_Format.md`, messages with `Message Type == 11` use the first byte of their payload to define a `Sub-Type`.
    5 
    6 ### `DONE` Sub-Payload (DLC = 3)
    7 
    8 *   **Sub-Type**: `0x01`
    9 
   10 | Byte(s)  | Field Name      | Description                                                 |
   11 |----------|-----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
   12 | `0`      | Sub-Type (`0x01`)| Identifies this frame as a `DONE` message.                    |
   13 | `1-2`    | **Low-Level** Command Code | The 16-bit code of the command that has finished.           |
   14 
   15 ### `DATA` Sub-Payload (DLC = 3-8)
   16 
   17 *   **Sub-Type**: `0x02`
   18 
   19 | Byte(s)  | Field Name      | Description                                                 |
   20 |----------|-----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
   21 | `0`      | Sub-Type (`0x02`)| Identifies this frame as a `DATA` message.                    |
   22 | `1`      | Sequence Info   | Contains sequence number and end-of-transmission flag.      |
   23 | `2-7`    | Data            | 1 to 6 bytes of payload data.                               |
   24 
   25 **Sequence Info Byte (Byte 1):**
   26 
   27 *   **Bit 7 (EOT)**: `1` if this is the last frame in the sequence; `0` otherwise.
   28 *   **Bits 6-0**: Sequence number (0-127). Increments for each frame in a multi-frame transfer.
   29 
   30 ### `LOG` Sub-Payload (DLC = 3-8)
   31 
   32 *   **Sub-Type**: `0x03`
   33 
   34 | Byte(s)  | Field Name      | Description                                                 |
   35 |----------|-----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
   36 | `0`      | Sub-Type (`0x03`)| Identifies this frame as a `LOG` message.                     |
   37 | `1`      | Log Level       | `1`=ERROR, `2`=WARN, `3`=INFO, `4`=DEBUG.                   |
   38 | `2-7`    | Log Message     | 1 to 6 bytes of a UTF-8 encoded string. Log messages longer than 6 bytes will be sent as multiple `LOG` frames. |

